<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Beiyang government</h1><p class="st-meta">1912 CE – 1928 CE · capital Beijing</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The internationally recognised government of the Republic of China based in Beijing, dominated first by Yuan Shikai and then by rival warlord cliques.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-shikai">Yuan Shikai</a>, commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beiyang-army">Beiyang Army</a>, the most modern Qing force, negotiated the abdication of the last emperor in 1912 and replaced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sun-yat-sen">Sun Yat-sen</a> as president of the new <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-china">Republic of China</a>, keeping the capital in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>. He crushed the Nationalists' <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-revolution">Second Revolution</a> of 1913 and governed increasingly as a dictator.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>After Yuan's failed attempt to restore the monarchy as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/empire-of-china-1915-1916">Empire of China</a> (1915-1916) and his death, control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> passed between military cliques: the Anhui clique of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duan-qirui">Duan Qirui</a>, the Zhili clique of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-kun">Cao Kun</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-peifu">Wu Peifu</a>, and the Fengtian clique of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-zuolin">Zhang Zuolin</a>. Cabinets and presidents changed rapidly, while provinces ruled themselves. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> in 1917, and anger at the peace settlement sparked the May Fourth Movement in 1919.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nationalist-government">Nationalist government</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-expedition">Northern Expedition</a> from 1926 defeated the northern warlords. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-zuolin">Zhang Zuolin</a> abandoned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> in June 1928 and was killed by a Japanese bomb; Beijing was renamed Beiping and the capital moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1912 CE – 1928 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:97.75%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1912 CE – 1928 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Beijing</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yuan Shikai, Duan Qirui, Zhang Zuolin</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Chinese folk religion, Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mandarin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Beiyang Government, Beijing government</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=beiyang-government" aria-label="Beiyang government on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7548 750 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Beiyang government lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7868 1006L8221 1549M7868 1006L8025 1580M7868 1006L7708 1003M7868 1006L8025 1580"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8221 1549h0M8025 1580h0M7708 1003h0M8025 1580h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7868 1006h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7868 1006h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Beijing. <a href="/a